review_comments.body:
The first pass can leave a redundant conjunct, though this is non-blocking. `PropagateExpression` rewrites against un-narrowed input statistics, turning a comparison earlier conjuncts would make always true into `constant_or_null(...)`, which the regular pass no longer folds. With these optimizers disabled, base drops the second conjunct; head keeps `(y > CAST(1 AS INTEGER)) OR constant_or_null(true, x, 0)`. I found no default-optimizer plan difference. Could we run the first pass only when `debug_verify_stats` is set, or propagate copies so the regular pass sees the original conjuncts?

```sql
SET disabled_optimizers = 'filter_pushdown,expression_rewriter,join_order';
CREATE TABLE prune_left(x INTEGER);
INSERT INTO prune_left VALUES (NULL), (0), (2);
CREATE TABLE prune_right(y INTEGER);
INSERT INTO prune_right VALUES (0), (2);
EXPLAIN SELECT count(*) FROM prune_left, prune_right WHERE x > 1 AND (x >= 0 OR y > 1);
```

